    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS, 1/1 test green \u2014 `AcceptanceTest` is the only test class).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented `telephoneDisplay` as the stored E.164 telephone formatted for humans, while `telephone` stays raw E.164.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n1. **`TelephoneDisplay.java`** (new helper) \u2014 formats an E.164 string as `country code + space + national digits grouped in threes`. It recognizes the same country codes the app normalizes to (`+61`, `+1`), so `+61412345678` \u2192 `+61 412 345 678`. Null/non-E.164 input is passed through unchanged.\n\n2. **`openapi.yml`** \u2014 added a read-only `telephoneDisplay` string property to the derived section of the `Owner` schema (so the generated `OwnerDto` gets the field), alongside the existing `displayName`/`initials`/etc.\n\n3. **`OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` for `telephoneDisplay` that computes it from `owner.getTelephone()` via `TelephoneDisplay.of(...)`.\n\nThe raw `telephone` field is untouched \u2014 the entity still stores and returns E.164 (`+61412345678`), and the new field is purely a derived display rendering, consistent with how the other derived fields (`displayName`, `checkDigit`, `locality`, etc.) are handled in this project.\n\nThe acceptance test `coreFormatsTelephoneDisplay` confirms both: `$.telephone` = `+61412345678` and `$.telephoneDisplay` = `+61 412 345 678`.",
